{
    "_doc": "Food skills (systems/foodSkills.js): farming, fishing and cooking, levelled 1-10 like diving (systems/practiceSkills.js). FARMING (systems/crops.js, ui/innerMapFarming.js): yield = % bigger harvests; dryDays = more dry days a crop bears before it wilts; frostDays = winter frost days a tender crop lives through (growing at the winter rate) before the frost takes it; speed = % quicker at tilling, sowing, watering and harvesting (the work and the clock both). xp: till / sow / water / harvest per cell, perUnit per unit brought in; legacy: an old save's player.skills.farming (0..10) becomes XP once. FISHING (ui/actionMenu/skills.js doFish, ui/mapTasks/wildTasks.js fish, player/seasonalWork.js iceFish): bites = more chance a cast gets a bite (percentage points); window = seconds more to strike; land = percentage points more to land a hooked fish; bigger = % chance a landed fish is the bigger kind (bigger: small fry -> common fish -> large cod); junk = % less weed and old boots; casts = more casts a day; deepReach (1) = casts reach deep water from any sea shore. catches: the fish by depth, each with minLevel (deep-water fish only for a practised angler); rarityWeights: the draw by rarity (luckRare / luckLegendary per point of luck). xp: perCast, by rarity per fish landed, snapped (a fish lost), quickShare of it on a quick trip, ice per fish through the ice. COOKING (player/crafting.js through trades.craftSkills, as systems/tradeSkills.js does for smithing: the Cook modal reads its level; the eat modal; player/core/needs.js): quality = craftsmanship added to the grade roll (finer dishes); waste = % of the makings lost when a dish spoils; minutes = time a dish takes; spare = % chance of an extra portion; hearty = % more hunger and energy from a cooked dish you eat; wellFed = after a cooked dish, hunger drains this % slower for wellFedHours. xp.craft: cooking XP per point of a recipe's xp; an old save's player.skills.cooking migrates. Inns: a keeper's own cooking level (seeded as an innkeeper) makes the meals there that much heartier (systems/hospitality.js). npc: levels by role and the daily XP of each trade.",
